+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+Apply RFC 6902 JSON Patch documents to JSON documents, so services can change stored records and payloads with a standard format and without mutating their inputs.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: applyPatch contract
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` SHALL return the document resulting from applying the operations of `patch` in order (RFC 6902 §3, §5). It SHALL NOT mutate `document` or `patch`, and the result SHALL NOT share mutable objects or arrays with either. If the patch is invalid or any operation fails it SHALL throw a `JsonPatchError` and no partial result is observable (RFC 6902 §5).
+
+#### Scenario: Inputs not mutated
+- **WHEN** a patch with add, remove and move operations is applied to a nested document
+- **THEN** the document and the patch deep-equal their original values afterwards
+
+#### Scenario: No aliasing
+- **WHEN** the result is modified after an `add` whose value is an object, or a `copy` of an object
+- **THEN** neither the patch value, the original document, nor the copied source changes
+
+#### Scenario: Empty patch
+- **WHEN** the patch is `[]`
+- **THEN** a value equal to the document is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Atomic failure
+- **WHEN** the second operation of a patch fails
+- **THEN** an error is thrown and the original document is unchanged
+
+### Requirement: Patch validation
+`patch` SHALL be an array of operation objects, each with a string `op` that is one of `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, `test` and a string `path` (RFC 6902 §3, §4). `add`, `replace` and `test` SHALL have a `value` member (`null` is a valid value); `move` and `copy` SHALL have a string `from`. Unknown additional members SHALL be ignored (§4). Invalid pointers SHALL be errors (RFC 6901 §3).
+
+#### Scenario: Patch is not an array
+- **WHEN** the patch is an object, `null`, a string or `undefined`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Bad operation object
+- **WHEN** an operation is `null`, an array, lacks `op` or `path`, has a non-string `op` or `path`, or has an unknown `op` such as `"merge"` or `"ADD"`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing value or from
+- **WHEN** `add`, `replace` or `test` has no `value`, or `move` or `copy` has no `from` or a non-string `from`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Null value allowed
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/a","value":null}` is applied to `{}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":null}`
+
+#### Scenario: Extra members and bad pointers
+- **WHEN** an operation has an extra member such as `"comment"`
+- **THEN** it is applied normally
+- **WHEN** a `path` or `from` is `"foo"` or contains `~2`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: add operation
+`add` SHALL set an object member (replacing an existing one) or insert into an array at an index in `0..length`, shifting later elements, or append with `-`; the parent of the target SHALL exist; an empty path SHALL replace the whole document (RFC 6902 §4.1).
+
+#### Scenario: Add object member
+- **WHEN** `add /b 2` is applied to `{"a":1}`, and `add /a 9` to `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** the results are `{"a":1,"b":2}` and `{"a":9}`
+
+#### Scenario: Add array element
+- **WHEN** `add /1 "x"` is applied to `["a","b"]`, `add /2 "x"` to `["a","b"]`, and `add /- "x"` to `["a","b"]`
+- **THEN** the results are `["a","x","b"]`, `["a","b","x"]` and `["a","b","x"]`
+
+#### Scenario: Add array errors
+- **WHEN** the index is greater than the length, negative, has a leading zero (`/01`), is not a number (`/x`), or the array is addressed with `-` as a non-final token
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Add to missing parent
+- **WHEN** `add /a/b 1` is applied to `{}`, or the parent is a scalar
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Add at root
+- **WHEN** `add "" [1]` is applied to `{"a":1}` (or to a scalar)
+- **THEN** the result is `[1]`
+
+#### Scenario: Empty and escaped keys
+- **WHEN** `add /` is applied with value 1 to `{}`, and `add /a~1b` and `add /m~0n` are applied
+- **THEN** the members are `""`, `"a/b"` and `"m~n"`
+
+### Requirement: remove operation
+`remove` SHALL delete the target, which MUST exist; removing an array element shifts later elements down (RFC 6902 §4.2). Removing the whole document (empty path) SHALL be an error, because RFC 6902 defines no result for it.
+
+#### Scenario: Remove member and element
+- **WHEN** `remove /a` is applied to `{"a":1,"b":2}`, and `remove /1` to `["a","b","c"]`
+- **THEN** the results are `{"b":2}` and `["a","c"]`
+
+#### Scenario: Remove missing target
+- **WHEN** the member does not exist, the index is out of range, the path is `/-`, or an intermediate is missing
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Remove root
+- **WHEN** `remove ""` is applied
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: replace operation
+`replace` SHALL replace the value at the target, which MUST exist (RFC 6902 §4.3); an empty path replaces the whole document.
+
+#### Scenario: Replace
+- **WHEN** `replace /a 2` is applied to `{"a":1}`, `replace /0 "z"` to `["a"]`, and `replace "" 5` to `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** the results are `{"a":2}`, `["z"]` and `5`
+
+#### Scenario: Replace missing target
+- **WHEN** the member is absent, the index equals the length, or the path is `/-`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: move operation
+`move` SHALL remove the value at `from` (which MUST exist) and add it at `path` as `add` would, with array indices in `path` interpreted after the removal. It is an error if `from` is a proper prefix of `path`, compared token by token; `from` equal to `path` is a no-op (RFC 6902 §4.4).
+
+#### Scenario: Move member
+- **WHEN** `move /a to /b/c` is applied to `{"a":1,"b":{}}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"b":{"c":1}}`
+
+#### Scenario: Move within array
+- **WHEN** `move from /0 path /2` is applied to `["a","b","c"]`, and `move from /2 path /0`
+- **THEN** the results are `["b","c","a"]` and `["c","a","b"]`
+
+#### Scenario: Move into own child
+- **WHEN** `move from /a path /a/b` is applied to `{"a":{}}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown, whereas `from /a path /ab` is not a prefix case and succeeds
+
+#### Scenario: Move to same location and missing source
+- **WHEN** `from` equals `path` and exists, the document is unchanged
+- **WHEN** `from` does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: copy operation
+`copy` SHALL add a deep copy of the value at `from` (which MUST exist) at `path` as `add` would (RFC 6902 §4.5).
+
+#### Scenario: Copy
+- **WHEN** `copy from /a path /b` is applied to `{"a":{"x":[1]}}` and the result's `/b/x` is then modified
+- **THEN** the result has equal `a` and `b` initially and `a` is unaffected by the modification
+
+#### Scenario: Copy errors
+- **WHEN** `from` does not exist or the target parent is missing
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: test operation
+`test` SHALL succeed only if the value at `path` equals `value` by JSON equality, otherwise an error is thrown (RFC 6902 §4.6). Equality: same JSON type; numbers by numeric value; strings by code units; arrays element-wise in order; objects with the same member names and equal values regardless of member order. The document is not changed.
+
+#### Scenario: Equal values
+- **WHEN** testing `{"a":1,"b":[1,{"c":null}]}` against the same value with members in a different order, or `1` against `1.0`
+- **THEN** the patch succeeds
+
+#### Scenario: Unequal values
+- **WHEN** testing `1` against `"1"`, `null` against `0`, `[1,2]` against `[2,1]`, `{"a":1}` against `{"a":1,"b":2}`, or `false` against `0`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing target and root
+- **WHEN** the path does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+- **WHEN** the path is `""`
+- **THEN** the whole document is compared
+
+#### Scenario: Failed test aborts patch
+- **WHEN** a `test` fails before an `add` in the same patch
+- **THEN** an error is thrown and the later operation has no effect
+
+### Requirement: Safe handling of hostile keys
+Operations SHALL treat `__proto__`, `constructor` and `prototype` as ordinary member names and SHALL NOT modify any prototype; only own members are addressable.
+
+#### Scenario: __proto__ member
+- **WHEN** `add /__proto__/polluted true` is applied to `{}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown and `Object.prototype.polluted` is undefined
+- **WHEN** `add /__proto__ {"x":1}` is applied to `{}`
+- **THEN** the result has an own member `__proto__` and `Object.getPrototypeOf(result)` is `Object.prototype`
+- **WHEN** a document parsed by `JSON.parse` with an own `__proto__` member is patched
+- **THEN** the member is preserved in the result as an own member
+
+#### Scenario: Inherited names are not members
+- **WHEN** `remove /toString` or `test /constructor` is applied to `{}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
